// A UNIFORM ENTRY PARAMETER's default value (t_4b54f26b A1).
//
// parser.cpp errored on any '=' in any parameter list, which refused the
// reference's own spelling on seven reference-SDK rows.  The reference's rule,
// measured: a default is legal on a uniform parameter of the SELECTED entry
// and on any parameter of a helper, and nowhere else (C1114).
//
// FOUR SPELLINGS, each covering something the others cannot, and all four
// produce the SAME 16-byte block - only the parser distinguishes them:
//   light  braced initialiser, the spelling the SDK sources actually use
//   Ka     a SCALAR default for a VECTOR.  Cg broadcasts it, so this means
//          (0.6,0.6,0.6).  The entry-parameter path stored what the
//          EXPRESSION held and produced (0.6,0,0,0) until this fixture caught
//          it - right in x, zero elsewhere, which renders as a plausible
//          darker colour rather than as anything obviously wrong.  The
//          file-scope path had learned the same lesson earlier.
//   l      the constructor spelling
//   s      a scalar default on a scalar, where no broadcast is involved
//
// Values measured on the reference, block AND ucode inline constant:
//   light [1,2,3,4]  Ka [0.6,0.6,0.6,0]  l [1,2,3,0]  s [2.5,0,0,0]
void main(
	float2 texcoord      : TEXCOORD0,
	uniform float4 light = {1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0},
	uniform float3 Ka    = 0.6f,
	uniform float3 l     = float3(1.0, 2.0, 3.0),
	uniform float  s     = 2.5,
	out float4 color_out : COLOR)
{
	color_out = light * float4(Ka + l, s) * texcoord.x;
}
